IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`

-- coa5-loss-of-office.l4: Companies Act 2006, Part 10, Chapter 4, "Payments for loss of office": ss 215 to 222 (lines 2822-2927 of
-- ukpga-2006-46.txt): what a payment for loss of office is (s 215), amounts taken to be such payments (s 216), the three requirements
-- of members' approval (ss 217 to 219), the exceptions (ss 220, 221) and the civil consequences (s 222).
--
-- SOURCE: a plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; not the official text.
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER: see coa5-loans-exceptions.l4 (JUST TRUE, JUST FALSE and NOTHING as the rule of 2026-10-29 reads them).
-- Where the text says "may not ... unless", the question is "does the bar apply": JUST TRUE when the unmet condition leaves the bar in
-- place, JUST FALSE when the "unless" condition is met (the bar lifts), NOTHING outside the kind of case the section speaks of.

§ `Chapter 4: payments for loss of office (ss 215 to 222)`

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 215 Payments for loss of office
-- ======================================================================================================================

DECLARE `s 215(1) nature of the payment` IS ONE OF
    `s 215(1)(a) compensation for loss of office as director of the company`
    `s 215(1)(b)(i) compensation for loss of any other office or employment in connection with the management of the affairs of the company`
    `s 215(1)(b)(ii) compensation for loss of any office (as director or otherwise) or employment in connection with the management of the affairs of a subsidiary undertaking of the company`
    `s 215(1)(c) consideration for or in connection with retirement from office as director of the company`
    `s 215(1)(d)(i) consideration for or in connection with retirement from any other office or employment in connection with the management of the affairs of the company`
    `s 215(1)(d)(ii) consideration for or in connection with retirement from any office (as director or otherwise) or employment in connection with the management of the affairs of a subsidiary undertaking of the company`
    `s 215(1) some other payment`

-- src:2824 | (1) In this Chapter a “payment for loss of office” means a payment made to a director or past director of a company—
-- src:2825 | (a) by way of compensation for loss of office as director of the company,
-- src:2826 | (b) by way of compensation for loss, while director of the company or in connection with his ceasing to be a director of it, of—
-- src:2827 | (i) any other office or employment in connection with the management of the affairs of the company, or
-- src:2828 | (ii) any office (as director or otherwise) or employment in connection with the management of the affairs of any subsidiary undertaking of the company,
-- src:2829 | (c) as consideration for or in connection with his retirement from his office as director of the company, or
-- src:2830 | (d) as consideration for or in connection with his retirement, while director of the company or in connection with his ceasing to be a director of it, from—
-- src:2831 | (i) any other office or employment in connection with the management of the affairs of the company, or
-- src:2832 | (ii) any office (as director or otherwise) or employment in connection with the management of the affairs of any subsidiary undertaking of the company.
@ref s 215(1) payment for loss of office (src:2824-2832)
GIVEN nature IS A `s 215(1) nature of the payment`
      `made to a director or past director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the loss or retirement was while director of the company or in connection with his ceasing to be a director of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(1) the payment is a payment for loss of office` MEANS
    IF NOT `made to a director or past director of the company`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a “payment for loss of office” means a payment made to a director or past director of a company"
    ELSE CONSIDER nature
         WHEN `s 215(1)(a) compensation for loss of office as director of the company` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 215(1)(c) consideration for or in connection with retirement from office as director of the company` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 215(1)(b)(i) compensation for loss of any other office or employment in connection with the management of the affairs of the company` THEN `s 215(1) the timing limb`
         WHEN `s 215(1)(b)(ii) compensation for loss of any office (as director or otherwise) or employment in connection with the management of the affairs of a subsidiary undertaking of the company` THEN `s 215(1) the timing limb`
         WHEN `s 215(1)(d)(i) consideration for or in connection with retirement from any other office or employment in connection with the management of the affairs of the company` THEN `s 215(1) the timing limb`
         WHEN `s 215(1)(d)(ii) consideration for or in connection with retirement from any office (as director or otherwise) or employment in connection with the management of the affairs of a subsidiary undertaking of the company` THEN `s 215(1) the timing limb`
         WHEN `s 215(1) some other payment` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "means a payment made to a director or past director of a company— (a) ... (b) ... (c) ... or (d) ..."
    WHERE
        `s 215(1) the timing limb` MEANS
            IF `the loss or retirement was while director of the company or in connection with his ceasing to be a director of it`
            THEN JUST TRUE
            ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "compensation for loss, while director of the company or in connection with his ceasing to be a director of it, of ..." (limbs (b) and (d))

-- src:2833 | (2) The references to compensation and consideration include benefits otherwise than in cash and references in this Chapter to payment have a corresponding meaning.
@ref s 215(2) benefits otherwise than in cash (src:2833-2833)
GIVEN `the benefit is otherwise than in cash` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(2) the benefit counts as compensation, consideration or payment` MEANS
    IF `the benefit is otherwise than in cash`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "The references to compensation and consideration include benefits otherwise than in cash"

DECLARE `s 215(3) the recipient` IS ONE OF
    `s 215(3)(a) a person connected with a director`
    `s 215(3)(b) any person at the direction of, or for the benefit of, a director or a person connected with him`
    `s 215(3) the director himself`
    `s 215(3) someone else`

-- src:2834 | (3) For the purposes of sections 217 to 221 (payments requiring members' approval)—
-- src:2835 | (a) payment to a person connected with a director, or
-- src:2836 | (b) payment to any person at the direction of, or for the benefit of, a director or a person connected with him,
-- src:2837 | is treated as payment to the director.
@ref s 215(3) payment to a connected person or at the director's direction (src:2834-2837)
GIVEN recipient IS A `s 215(3) the recipient`
      `the payment is one within sections 217 to 221` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(3) the payment is treated as payment to the director` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the payment is one within sections 217 to 221`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of sections 217 to 221 (payments requiring members' approval)"
        IF recipient EQUALS `s 215(3)(a) a person connected with a director` OR recipient EQUALS `s 215(3)(b) any person at the direction of, or for the benefit of, a director or a person connected with him`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) payment to a person connected with a director, or (b) payment to any person at the direction of, or for the benefit of, a director or a person connected with him, is treated as payment to the director"

-- src:2838 | (4) References in those sections to payment by a person include payment by another person at the direction of, or on behalf of, the person referred to.
@ref s 215(4) payment by another person at the direction of the person referred to (src:2838-2838)
GIVEN `the payment is made by another person at the direction of, or on behalf of, the person referred to` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(4) the payment is treated as a payment by the person` MEANS
    IF `the payment is made by another person at the direction of, or on behalf of, the person referred to`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "References in those sections to payment by a person include payment by another person at the direction of, or on behalf of, the person referred to"

-- src:2839 | (5) Nothing in this section or sections 216 to 222 applies in relation to a payment for loss of office to a director of a quoted company ... other than a payment to which section 226C does not apply by virtue of section 226D(6).
@ref s 215(5) quoted companies (src:2839-2839)
GIVEN `the payment is to a director of a quoted company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a payment to which section 226C does not apply by virtue of section 226D(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 215(5) section 215 and sections 216 to 222 apply to the payment` MEANS
    IF `the payment is to a director of a quoted company` AND (NOT `it is a payment to which section 226C does not apply by virtue of section 226D(6)`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section or sections 216 to 222 applies in relation to a payment for loss of office to a director of a quoted company"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "other than a payment to which section 226C does not apply by virtue of section 226D(6)" (and the section speaks of no payment other than one to a director of a quoted company)

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 216 Amounts taken to be payments for loss of office
-- ======================================================================================================================

-- src:2842 | (1) This section applies where in connection with any such transfer as is mentioned in section 218 or 219 (payment in connection with transfer of undertaking, property or shares) a director of the company—
-- src:2843 | (a) is to cease to hold office, or
-- src:2844 | (b) is to cease to be the holder of—
-- src:2845 | (i) any other office or employment in connection with the management of the affairs of the company, or
-- src:2846 | (ii) any office (as director or otherwise) or employment in connection with the management of the affairs of any subsidiary undertaking of the company.
@ref s 216(1) application (src:2842-2846)
GIVEN `in connection with a transfer mentioned in section 218 or 219` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a director of the company is to cease to hold office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a director of the company is to cease to be the holder of any other office or employment in connection with the management of the affairs of the company or of any office or employment in connection with the management of the affairs of a subsidiary undertaking` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 216(1) this section applies` MEANS
    IF `in connection with a transfer mentioned in section 218 or 219` AND (`a director of the company is to cease to hold office` OR `a director of the company is to cease to be the holder of any other office or employment in connection with the management of the affairs of the company or of any office or employment in connection with the management of the affairs of a subsidiary undertaking`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where in connection with any such transfer as is mentioned in section 218 or 219 a director of the company— (a) is to cease to hold office, or (b) is to cease to be the holder of"

-- src:2848 | (a) the price to be paid to the director for any shares in the company held by him is in excess of the price which could at the time have been obtained by other holders of like shares, or
@ref s 216(2)(a) excess price for shares (src:2848-2848)
GIVEN `s 216(1) this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the price to be paid to the director for shares in the company held by him` IS A NUMBER
      `the price which could at the time have been obtained by other holders of like shares` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 216(2)(a) the excess taken to have been a payment for loss of office` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 216(1) this section applies` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the section applies is not known
        IF `s 216(1) this section applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies where"
        IF `the price to be paid to the director for shares in the company held by him` GREATER THAN `the price which could at the time have been obtained by other holders of like shares`
        THEN JUST (`the price to be paid to the director for shares in the company held by him` MINUS `the price which could at the time have been obtained by other holders of like shares`)
        OTHERWISE JUST 0 -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If in connection with any such transfer— (a) the price to be paid to the director for any shares in the company held by him is in excess of the price which could at the time have been obtained by other holders of like shares" (no excess, so nothing is taken to be a payment)

-- src:2849 | (b) any valuable consideration is given to the director by a person other than the company,
-- src:2850 | the excess or, as the case may be, the money value of the consideration is taken for the purposes of those sections to have been a payment for loss of office.
@ref s 216(2)(b) valuable consideration given by another person (src:2849-2850)
GIVEN `s 216(1) this section applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `valuable consideration is given to the director by a person other than the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the money value of the consideration` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 216(2)(b) the money value taken to have been a payment for loss of office` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 216(1) this section applies` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): whether the section applies is not known
        IF `s 216(1) this section applies` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies where"
        IF `valuable consideration is given to the director by a person other than the company`
        THEN JUST `the money value of the consideration`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any valuable consideration is given to the director by a person other than the company"

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 217 Payment by company: requirement of members' approval
-- ======================================================================================================================

-- src:2859 | (4) No approval is required under this section on the part of the members of a body corporate that—
-- src:2860 | (a) is not a UK-registered company, or
-- src:2861 | (b) is a wholly-owned subsidiary of another body corporate.
@ref s 217(4) approval not required of members of certain bodies corporate (src:2859-2861)
GIVEN `the body corporate is a UK-registered company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body corporate is a wholly-owned subsidiary of another body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 217(4) no approval is required under section 217 on the part of the members of the body corporate` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the body corporate is a UK-registered company`) OR `the body corporate is a wholly-owned subsidiary of another body corporate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a body corporate that— (a) is not a UK-registered company, or (b) is a wholly-owned subsidiary of another body corporate"

-- src:2852 | (1) A company may not make a payment for loss of office to a director of the company unless the payment has been approved by a resolution of the members of the company.
@ref s 217(1) a payment to a director of the company needs the members' approval (src:2852-2852)
GIVEN `the payment is a payment for loss of office to a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment has been approved by a resolution of the members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 217(4) for the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 217(1) the company may not make the payment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the payment is a payment for loss of office to a director of the company`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a payment for loss of office to a director of the company"
        IF `s 217(4) for the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No approval is required under this section on the part of the members of a body corporate that" (the bar does not run to the company)
        IF `the payment has been approved by a resolution of the members of the company`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may not make a payment for loss of office to a director of the company unless the payment has been approved by a resolution of the members of the company"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE -- "A company may not make a payment for loss of office to a director of the company"

-- src:2853 | (2) A company may not make a payment for loss of office to a director of its holding company unless the payment has been approved by a resolution of the members of each of those companies.
@ref s 217(2) a payment to a director of its holding company needs the approval of each company's members (src:2853-2853)
GIVEN `the payment is a payment for loss of office to a director of its holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `approved by a resolution of the members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `approved by a resolution of the members of the holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 217(4) for the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 217(4) for the holding company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 217(2) the company may not make the payment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the payment is a payment for loss of office to a director of its holding company`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a payment for loss of office to a director of its holding company"
        IF (`approved by a resolution of the members of the company` OR `s 217(4) for the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
           AND (`approved by a resolution of the members of the holding company` OR `s 217(4) for the holding company` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the payment has been approved by a resolution of the members of each of those companies" (where approval is not required of a body's members, s 217(4), it is not needed)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE -- "A company may not make a payment for loss of office to a director of its holding company"

-- The twin of s 217(1) and (2) as a duty: the Company SHANT make the payment where the approval is missing. A trace cannot be asserted on
-- the stable binary (see NOTES.md, "What the stable binary does not accept"), so the decision functions above carry the assertions.
DECLARE `s 217 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 217 make the payment for loss of office`

-- src:2852 | (1) A company may not make a payment for loss of office to a director of the company unless the payment has been approved by a resolution of the members of the company.
-- src:2853 | (2) A company may not make a payment for loss of office to a director of its holding company unless the payment has been approved by a resolution of the members of each of those companies.
@ref s 217(1) and (2) the company's duty not to make the payment (src:2852-2853)
GIVEN `the bar applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 217 action`
`s 217(1) and (2) the company's duty not to make the payment` MEANS
    IF `the bar applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY Company
         SHANT `s 217 make the payment for loss of office`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 217: a payment for loss of office was made without the approval of a resolution of the members"
    ELSE FULFILLED

DECLARE `s 217(3) memorandum` HAS
    `s 217(3) made available` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 217(3) in the case of a written resolution, sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time the proposed resolution is sent or submitted to him` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 217(3) in the case of a meeting, the first day it was available for inspection at the registered office` IS A DATE
    `s 217(3) in the case of a meeting, the date of the meeting` IS A DATE
    `s 217(3) in the case of a meeting, available for inspection at the meeting itself` IS A BOOLEAN

-- "not less than 15 days ending with the date of the meeting": the days from the first day of inspection to the date of the meeting, both counted, are at least 15.
-- src:2854 | (3) A resolution approving a payment to which this section applies must not be passed unless a memorandum setting out particulars of the proposed payment (including its amount) is made available to the members of the company whose approval is sought—
-- src:2855 | (a) in the case of a written resolution, by being sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time at which the proposed resolution is sent or submitted to him;
-- src:2856 | (b) in the case of a resolution at a meeting, by being made available for inspection by the members both—
-- src:2857 | (i) at the company's registered office for not less than 15 days ending with the date of the meeting, and
-- src:2858 | (ii) at the meeting itself.
@ref s 217(3) the memorandum (src:2854-2858)
GIVEN way IS A `Way a resolution is passed`
      `the resolution approves a payment to which this section applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      memo IS A `s 217(3) memorandum`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 217(3) the resolution approving the payment must not be passed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the resolution approves a payment to which this section applies`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A resolution approving a payment to which this section applies"
        IF NOT memo's `s 217(3) made available`
        THEN JUST TRUE -- "must not be passed unless a memorandum setting out particulars of the proposed payment (including its amount) is made available"
        IF way EQUALS `as a written resolution`
        THEN IF memo's `s 217(3) in the case of a written resolution, sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time the proposed resolution is sent or submitted to him`
             THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless a memorandum ... is made available ... (a) in the case of a written resolution, by being sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time at which the proposed resolution is sent or submitted to him"
             ELSE JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
             IF memo's `s 217(3) in the case of a meeting, the first day it was available for inspection at the registered office` PLUS 14 AT MOST memo's `s 217(3) in the case of a meeting, the date of the meeting`
                AND memo's `s 217(3) in the case of a meeting, available for inspection at the meeting itself`
             THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) in the case of a resolution at a meeting, by being made available for inspection by the members both— (i) at the company's registered office for not less than 15 days ending with the date of the meeting, and (ii) at the meeting itself"
             ELSE JUST TRUE

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 218 Payment in connection with transfer of undertaking etc: requirement of members' approval
-- ======================================================================================================================

-- src:2870 | (4) No approval is required under this section on the part of the members of a body corporate that—
-- src:2871 | (a) is not a UK-registered company, or
-- src:2872 | (b) is a wholly-owned subsidiary of another body corporate.
@ref s 218(4) approval not required of members of certain bodies corporate (src:2870-2872)
GIVEN `the body corporate is a UK-registered company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body corporate is a wholly-owned subsidiary of another body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 218(4) no approval is required under section 218 on the part of the members of the body corporate` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the body corporate is a UK-registered company`) OR `the body corporate is a wholly-owned subsidiary of another body corporate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a body corporate that— (a) is not a UK-registered company, or (b) is a wholly-owned subsidiary of another body corporate"

-- src:2863 | (1) No payment for loss of office may be made by any person to a director of a company in connection with the transfer of the whole or any part of the undertaking or property of the company unless the payment has been approved by a resolution of the members of the company.
@ref s 218(1) a payment in connection with a transfer of the company's undertaking or property (src:2863-2863)
GIVEN `the payment is made to a director of the company in connection with the transfer of the whole or any part of the undertaking or property of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment has been approved by a resolution of the members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 218(4) for the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 218(1) no person may make the payment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the payment is made to a director of the company in connection with the transfer of the whole or any part of the undertaking or property of the company`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to a director of a company in connection with the transfer of the whole or any part of the undertaking or property of the company"
        IF `s 218(4) for the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No approval is required under this section on the part of the members of a body corporate that"
        IF `the payment has been approved by a resolution of the members of the company`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the payment has been approved by a resolution of the members of the company"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE -- "No payment for loss of office may be made by any person to a director of a company in connection with the transfer of the whole or any part of the undertaking or property of the company"

-- src:2864 | (2) No payment for loss of office may be made by any person to a director of a company in connection with the transfer of the whole or any part of the undertaking or property of a subsidiary of the company unless the payment has been approved by a resolution of the members of each of the companies.
@ref s 218(2) a payment in connection with a transfer of a subsidiary's undertaking or property (src:2864-2864)
GIVEN `the payment is made to a director of a company in connection with the transfer of the whole or any part of the undertaking or property of a subsidiary of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `approved by a resolution of the members of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `approved by a resolution of the members of the subsidiary's parent company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 218(4) for the company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 218(4) for the subsidiary's parent company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 218(2) no person may make the payment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the payment is made to a director of a company in connection with the transfer of the whole or any part of the undertaking or property of a subsidiary of the company`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in connection with the transfer of the whole or any part of the undertaking or property of a subsidiary of the company"
        IF (`approved by a resolution of the members of the company` OR `s 218(4) for the company` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
           AND (`approved by a resolution of the members of the subsidiary's parent company` OR `s 218(4) for the subsidiary's parent company` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the payment has been approved by a resolution of the members of each of the companies"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE -- "No payment for loss of office may be made by any person to a director of a company in connection with the transfer of ... a subsidiary of the company"

DECLARE `s 218(3) memorandum` HAS
    `s 218(3) made available` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 218(3) in the case of a written resolution, sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time the proposed resolution is sent or submitted to him` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 218(3) in the case of a meeting, the first day it was available for inspection at the registered office` IS A DATE
    `s 218(3) in the case of a meeting, the date of the meeting` IS A DATE
    `s 218(3) in the case of a meeting, available for inspection at the meeting itself` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2865 | (3) A resolution approving a payment to which this section applies must not be passed unless a memorandum setting out particulars of the proposed payment (including its amount) is made available to the members of the company whose approval is sought—
-- src:2866 | (a) in the case of a written resolution, by being sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time at which the proposed resolution is sent or submitted to him;
-- src:2867 | (b) in the case of a resolution at a meeting, by being made available for inspection by the members both—
-- src:2868 | (i) at the company's registered office for not less than 15 days ending with the date of the meeting, and
-- src:2869 | (ii) at the meeting itself.
@ref s 218(3) the memorandum (src:2865-2869)
GIVEN way IS A `Way a resolution is passed`
      `the resolution approves a payment to which this section applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      memo IS A `s 218(3) memorandum`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 218(3) the resolution approving the payment must not be passed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the resolution approves a payment to which this section applies`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A resolution approving a payment to which this section applies"
        IF NOT memo's `s 218(3) made available`
        THEN JUST TRUE -- "must not be passed unless a memorandum setting out particulars of the proposed payment (including its amount) is made available"
        IF way EQUALS `as a written resolution`
        THEN IF memo's `s 218(3) in the case of a written resolution, sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time the proposed resolution is sent or submitted to him`
             THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless a memorandum ... is made available ... (a) in the case of a written resolution, by being sent or submitted to every eligible member"
             ELSE JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
             IF memo's `s 218(3) in the case of a meeting, the first day it was available for inspection at the registered office` PLUS 14 AT MOST memo's `s 218(3) in the case of a meeting, the date of the meeting`
                AND memo's `s 218(3) in the case of a meeting, available for inspection at the meeting itself`
             THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) in the case of a resolution at a meeting, by being made available for inspection by the members both— (i) at the company's registered office for not less than 15 days ending with the date of the meeting, and (ii) at the meeting itself"
             ELSE JUST TRUE

-- The presumption of s 218(5): "except in so far as the contrary is shown". The text sets the arrangement window as "as part of the agreement for the
-- transfer in question, or within one year before or two years after that agreement". "In so far as" is a partial rebuttal: this function asks only
-- whether the presumption holds for the payment, the contrary having been shown or not (fork F-218-1).
-- src:2873 | (5) A payment made in pursuance of an arrangement—
-- src:2874 | (a) entered into as part of the agreement for the transfer in question, or within one year before or two years after that agreement, and
-- src:2875 | (b) to which the company whose undertaking or property is transferred, or any person to whom the transfer is made, is privy,
-- src:2876 | is presumed, except in so far as the contrary is shown, to be a payment to which this section applies.
@ref s 218(5) presumption (src:2873-2876)
GIVEN `the arrangement was entered into as part of the agreement for the transfer in question` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the arrangement was entered into` IS A DATE
      `the date of the agreement for the transfer in question` IS A DATE
      `the company whose undertaking or property is transferred, or a person to whom the transfer is made, is privy to the arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is shown` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 218(5) the payment is presumed to be a payment to which section 218 applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the company whose undertaking or property is transferred, or a person to whom the transfer is made, is privy to the arrangement`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) to which the company whose undertaking or property is transferred, or any person to whom the transfer is made, is privy"
        IF NOT (   `the arrangement was entered into as part of the agreement for the transfer in question`
                OR (`add years` `the date the arrangement was entered into` 1 AT LEAST `the date of the agreement for the transfer in question` AND `the date the arrangement was entered into` AT MOST `add years` `the date of the agreement for the transfer in question` 2))
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) entered into as part of the agreement for the transfer in question, or within one year before or two years after that agreement"
        IF `the contrary is shown`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is presumed, except in so far as the contrary is shown"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 219 Payment in connection with share transfer: requirement of members' approval
-- ======================================================================================================================

-- src:2889 | (6) No approval is required under this section on the part of shareholders in a body corporate that—
-- src:2890 | (a) is not a UK-registered company, or
-- src:2891 | (b) is a wholly-owned subsidiary of another body corporate.
@ref s 219(6) approval not required of shareholders in certain bodies corporate (src:2889-2891)
GIVEN `the body corporate is a UK-registered company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body corporate is a wholly-owned subsidiary of another body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 219(6) no approval is required under section 219 on the part of the shareholders in the body corporate` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the body corporate is a UK-registered company`) OR `the body corporate is a wholly-owned subsidiary of another body corporate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "shareholders in a body corporate that— (a) is not a UK-registered company, or (b) is a wholly-owned subsidiary of another body corporate"

-- "The relevant shareholders are the holders of the shares to which the bid relates and any holders of shares of the same class as any of those shares."
-- The same-class answer is s 629's (coa14): an input.
-- src:2879 | (2) The relevant shareholders are the holders of the shares to which the bid relates and any holders of shares of the same class as any of those shares.
@ref s 219(2) the relevant shareholders (src:2879-2879)
GIVEN `holds shares to which the bid relates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 629 holds shares of the same class as any of those shares` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 219(2) the holder is one of the relevant shareholders` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `holds shares to which the bid relates` OR `s 629 holds shares of the same class as any of those shares` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 629 holds shares of the same class as any of those shares` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether shares are of the same class is s 629's answer
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "The relevant shareholders are the holders of the shares to which the bid relates and any holders of shares of the same class" (no "only")

-- src:2878 | (1) No payment for loss of office may be made by any person to a director of a company in connection with a transfer of shares in the company, or in a subsidiary of the company, resulting from a takeover bid unless the payment has been approved by a resolution of the relevant shareholders.
@ref s 219(1) a payment in connection with a transfer of shares resulting from a takeover bid (src:2878-2878)
GIVEN `the payment is made to a director of a company in connection with a transfer of shares in the company, or in a subsidiary of the company, resulting from a takeover bid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payment has been approved by a resolution of the relevant shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 219(1) no person may make the payment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the payment is made to a director of a company in connection with a transfer of shares in the company, or in a subsidiary of the company, resulting from a takeover bid`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in connection with a transfer of shares in the company, or in a subsidiary of the company, resulting from a takeover bid"
        IF `the payment has been approved by a resolution of the relevant shareholders`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the payment has been approved by a resolution of the relevant shareholders"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE -- "No payment for loss of office may be made by any person to a director of a company in connection with a transfer of shares"

DECLARE `s 219(3) memorandum` HAS
    `s 219(3) made available` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 219(3) in the case of a written resolution, sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time the proposed resolution is sent or submitted to him` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 219(3) in the case of a meeting, the first day it was available for inspection at the registered office` IS A DATE
    `s 219(3) in the case of a meeting, the date of the meeting` IS A DATE
    `s 219(3) in the case of a meeting, available for inspection at the meeting itself` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:2880 | (3) A resolution approving a payment to which this section applies must not be passed unless a memorandum setting out particulars of the proposed payment (including its amount) is made available to the members of the company whose approval is sought—
-- src:2881 | (a) in the case of a written resolution, by being sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time at which the proposed resolution is sent or submitted to him;
-- src:2882 | (b) in the case of a resolution at a meeting, by being made available for inspection by the members both—
-- src:2883 | (i) at the company's registered office for not less than 15 days ending with the date of the meeting, and
-- src:2884 | (ii) at the meeting itself.
@ref s 219(3) the memorandum (src:2880-2884)
GIVEN way IS A `Way a resolution is passed`
      `the resolution approves a payment to which this section applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      memo IS A `s 219(3) memorandum`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 219(3) the resolution approving the payment must not be passed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the resolution approves a payment to which this section applies`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A resolution approving a payment to which this section applies"
        IF NOT memo's `s 219(3) made available`
        THEN JUST TRUE -- "must not be passed unless a memorandum setting out particulars of the proposed payment (including its amount) is made available"
        IF way EQUALS `as a written resolution`
        THEN IF memo's `s 219(3) in the case of a written resolution, sent or submitted to every eligible member at or before the time the proposed resolution is sent or submitted to him`
             THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless a memorandum ... is made available ... (a) in the case of a written resolution, by being sent or submitted to every eligible member"
             ELSE JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
             IF memo's `s 219(3) in the case of a meeting, the first day it was available for inspection at the registered office` PLUS 14 AT MOST memo's `s 219(3) in the case of a meeting, the date of the meeting`
                AND memo's `s 219(3) in the case of a meeting, available for inspection at the meeting itself`
             THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) in the case of a resolution at a meeting, by being made available for inspection by the members both— (i) at the company's registered office for not less than 15 days ending with the date of the meeting, and (ii) at the meeting itself"
             ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (4): the offeror and its associates (s 988, coa21's answer) may not vote, but keep rights to a copy, notice, attendance, speech and a count towards the quorum.
-- src:2885 | (4) Neither the person making the offer, nor any associate of his (as defined in section 988), is entitled to vote on the resolution, but—
@ref s 219(4) the offeror and its associates may not vote (src:2885-2885)
GIVEN `the person is the person making the offer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 988 the person is an associate of the person making the offer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 219(4) the person is entitled to vote on the resolution` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is the person making the offer` OR `s 988 the person is an associate of the person making the offer` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Neither the person making the offer, nor any associate of his (as defined in section 988), is entitled to vote on the resolution"
        IF `s 988 the person is an associate of the person making the offer` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is an associate is s 988's answer
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): this subsection says nothing of who else may vote

-- src:2886 | (a) where the resolution is proposed as a written resolution, they are entitled (if they would otherwise be so entitled) to be sent a copy of it, and
@ref s 219(4)(a) written resolution: still entitled to a copy (src:2886-2886)
GIVEN `the person is the person making the offer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 988 the person is an associate of the person making the offer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the resolution is proposed as a written resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person would otherwise be entitled to be sent a copy of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 219(4)(a) the person is entitled to be sent a copy of the written resolution` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`the person is the person making the offer` OR `s 988 the person is an associate of the person making the offer` EQUALS JUST TRUE)) OR (NOT `the resolution is proposed as a written resolution`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "where the resolution is proposed as a written resolution, they are entitled (if they would otherwise be so entitled) to be sent a copy of it"
        IF `the person would otherwise be entitled to be sent a copy of it`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "they are entitled (if they would otherwise be so entitled) to be sent a copy of it"

-- src:2887 | (b) at any meeting to consider the resolution they are entitled (if they would otherwise be so entitled) to be given notice of the meeting, to attend and speak and if present (in person or by proxy) to count towards the quorum.
@ref s 219(4)(b) meeting: still entitled to notice, to attend and speak, and to count towards the quorum (src:2887-2887)
GIVEN `the person is the person making the offer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 988 the person is an associate of the person making the offer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the resolution is to be considered at a meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person would otherwise be entitled to be given notice of the meeting, to attend and speak and if present (in person or by proxy) to count towards the quorum` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 219(4)(b) the person is entitled to notice of the meeting, to attend and speak and, if present, to count towards the quorum` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`the person is the person making the offer` OR `s 988 the person is an associate of the person making the offer` EQUALS JUST TRUE)) OR (NOT `the resolution is to be considered at a meeting`)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "at any meeting to consider the resolution they are entitled (if they would otherwise be so entitled) to be given notice of the meeting, to attend and speak and if present (in person or by proxy) to count towards the quorum"
        IF `the person would otherwise be entitled to be given notice of the meeting, to attend and speak and if present (in person or by proxy) to count towards the quorum`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "they are entitled (if they would otherwise be so entitled)"

-- src:2888 | (5) If at a meeting to consider the resolution a quorum is not present, and after the meeting has been adjourned to a later date a quorum is again not present, the payment is (for the purposes of this section) deemed to have been approved.
@ref s 219(5) deemed approval where no quorum twice (src:2888-2888)
GIVEN `a quorum is not present at a meeting to consider the resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meeting has been adjourned to a later date and a quorum is again not present` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 219(5) the payment is deemed to have been approved` MEANS
    IF `a quorum is not present at a meeting to consider the resolution` AND `the meeting has been adjourned to a later date and a quorum is again not present`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If at a meeting to consider the resolution a quorum is not present, and after the meeting has been adjourned to a later date a quorum is again not present, the payment is (for the purposes of this section) deemed to have been approved"

-- src:2892 | (7) A payment made in pursuance of an arrangement—
-- src:2893 | (a) entered into as part of the agreement for the transfer in question, or within one year before or two years after that agreement, and
-- src:2894 | (b) to which the company whose shares are the subject of the bid, or any person to whom the transfer is made, is privy,
-- src:2895 | is presumed, except in so far as the contrary is shown, to be a payment to which this section applies.
@ref s 219(7) presumption (src:2892-2895)
GIVEN `the arrangement was entered into as part of the agreement for the transfer in question` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the arrangement was entered into` IS A DATE
      `the date of the agreement for the transfer in question` IS A DATE
      `the company whose shares are the subject of the bid, or a person to whom the transfer is made, is privy to the arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is shown` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 219(7) the payment is presumed to be a payment to which section 219 applies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the company whose shares are the subject of the bid, or a person to whom the transfer is made, is privy to the arrangement`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(b) to which the company whose shares are the subject of the bid, or any person to whom the transfer is made, is privy"
        IF NOT (   `the arrangement was entered into as part of the agreement for the transfer in question`
                OR (`add years` `the date the arrangement was entered into` 1 AT LEAST `the date of the agreement for the transfer in question` AND `the date the arrangement was entered into` AT MOST `add years` `the date of the agreement for the transfer in question` 2))
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) entered into as part of the agreement for the transfer in question, or within one year before or two years after that agreement"
        IF `the contrary is shown`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is presumed, except in so far as the contrary is shown"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 220 Exception for payments in discharge of legal obligations etc
-- ======================================================================================================================

-- src:2902 | (2) In relation to a payment within section 217 (payment by company) an existing legal obligation means an obligation of the company, or any body corporate associated with it, that was not entered into in connection with, or in consequence of, the event giving rise to the payment for loss of office.
@ref s 220(2) existing legal obligation, for a payment within section 217 (src:2902-2902)
GIVEN `s 256(a) the bodies corporate are associated` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is an obligation of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was not entered into in connection with, or in consequence of, the event giving rise to the payment for loss of office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 220(2) the obligation is an existing legal obligation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `it was not entered into in connection with, or in consequence of, the event giving rise to the payment for loss of office`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an existing legal obligation means an obligation of the company, or any body corporate associated with it, that was not entered into in connection with, or in consequence of, the event giving rise to the payment for loss of office"
        IF `it is an obligation of the company` OR `s 256(a) the bodies corporate are associated` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 256(a) the bodies corporate are associated` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the body corporate is associated with the company is s 256's answer
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an existing legal obligation means an obligation of the company, or any body corporate associated with it"

-- src:2903 | (3) In relation to a payment within section 218 or 219 (payment in connection with transfer of undertaking, property or shares) an existing legal obligation means an obligation of the person making the payment that was not entered into for the purposes of, in connection with or in consequence of, the transfer in question.
@ref s 220(3) existing legal obligation, for a payment within section 218 or 219 (src:2903-2903)
GIVEN `it is an obligation of the person making the payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was not entered into for the purposes of, in connection with or in consequence of, the transfer in question` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 220(3) the obligation is an existing legal obligation` MEANS
    IF `it is an obligation of the person making the payment` AND `it was not entered into for the purposes of, in connection with or in consequence of, the transfer in question`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "an existing legal obligation means an obligation of the person making the payment that was not entered into for the purposes of, in connection with or in consequence of, the transfer in question"

DECLARE `s 220(4) the sections the payment is within` IS ONE OF
    `s 220(4) section 217 only`
    `s 220(4) section 218 only`
    `s 220(4) section 219 only`
    `s 220(4) both section 217 and section 218`
    `s 220(4) both section 217 and section 219`

DECLARE `s 220(4) the definition that applies` IS ONE OF
    `s 220(4) subsection (2) applies`
    `s 220(4) subsection (3) applies`

-- src:2904 | (4) In the case of a payment within both section 217 and section 218, or within both section 217 and section 219, subsection (2) above applies and not subsection (3).
@ref s 220(4) payments within two sections (src:2904-2904)
GIVEN within IS A `s 220(4) the sections the payment is within`
GIVETH A `s 220(4) the definition that applies`
`s 220(4) which definition of an existing legal obligation applies` MEANS
    CONSIDER within
    WHEN `s 220(4) section 217 only` THEN `s 220(4) subsection (2) applies` -- s 220(2): "In relation to a payment within section 217"
    WHEN `s 220(4) section 218 only` THEN `s 220(4) subsection (3) applies` -- s 220(3): "In relation to a payment within section 218 or 219"
    WHEN `s 220(4) section 219 only` THEN `s 220(4) subsection (3) applies`
    WHEN `s 220(4) both section 217 and section 218` THEN `s 220(4) subsection (2) applies` -- "subsection (2) above applies and not subsection (3)"
    WHEN `s 220(4) both section 217 and section 219` THEN `s 220(4) subsection (2) applies`

DECLARE `s 220(1) ground` IS ONE OF
    `s 220(1)(a) in discharge of an existing legal obligation`
    `s 220(1)(b) by way of damages for breach of such an obligation`
    `s 220(1)(c) by way of settlement or compromise of any claim arising in connection with the termination of a person's office or employment`
    `s 220(1)(d) by way of pension in respect of past services`
    `s 220(1) some other ground`

-- src:2897 | (1) Approval is not required under section 217, 218 or 219 (payments requiring members' approval) for a payment made in good faith—
-- src:2898 | (a) in discharge of an existing legal obligation (as defined below),
-- src:2899 | (b) by way of damages for breach of such an obligation,
-- src:2900 | (c) by way of settlement or compromise of any claim arising in connection with the termination of a person's office or employment, or
-- src:2901 | (d) by way of pension in respect of past services.
@ref s 220(1) payments in discharge of legal obligations etc (src:2897-2901)
GIVEN ground IS A `s 220(1) ground`
      `the payment was made in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the obligation is an existing legal obligation` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 220(1) approval under section 217, 218 or 219 is not required by this section` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the payment was made in good faith`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for a payment made in good faith"
        IF ground EQUALS `s 220(1) some other ground`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) in discharge of an existing legal obligation ... (b) ... (c) ... or (d) by way of pension in respect of past services"
        IF ground EQUALS `s 220(1)(c) by way of settlement or compromise of any claim arising in connection with the termination of a person's office or employment` OR ground EQUALS `s 220(1)(d) by way of pension in respect of past services`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the obligation is an existing legal obligation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the obligation is an existing legal obligation` EQUALS JUST FALSE
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) in discharge of an existing legal obligation (as defined below), (b) by way of damages for breach of such an obligation" (an obligation that is not an existing legal obligation is outside limbs (a) and (b))
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the obligation is an existing legal obligation is not known

-- src:2905 | (5) A payment part of which falls within subsection (1) above and part of which does not is treated as if the parts were separate payments.
@ref s 220(5) part of a payment (src:2905-2905)
GIVEN `the amount of the whole payment` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the part that falls within subsection (1)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 220(5) the amount of the separate payment that is not within subsection (1)` MEANS
    `the amount of the whole payment` MINUS `the amount of the part that falls within subsection (1)`

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 221 Exception for small payments
-- ======================================================================================================================

-- src:2907 | (1) Approval is not required under section 217, 218 or 219 (payments requiring members' approval) if—
-- src:2908 | (a) the payment in question is made by the company or any of its subsidiaries, and
-- src:2909 | (b) the amount or value of the payment, together with the amount or value of any other relevant payments, does not exceed £200.
@ref s 221(1) the sum (src:2907-2909)
`s 221(1) the sum in pounds` MEANS 200

-- src:2911 | (3) Where the payment in question is one to which section 217 (payment by company) applies, the conditions are that the other payment was or is paid—
-- src:2912 | (a) by the company making the payment in question or any of its subsidiaries,
-- src:2913 | (b) to the director to whom that payment is made, and
-- src:2914 | (c) in connection with the same event.
@ref s 221(3) other relevant payments where section 217 applies (src:2911-2914)
GIVEN `paid by the company making the payment in question or any of its subsidiaries` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paid to the director to whom that payment is made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paid in connection with the same event` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 221(3) the conditions are met` MEANS
    IF `paid by the company making the payment in question or any of its subsidiaries` AND `paid to the director to whom that payment is made` AND `paid in connection with the same event`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the conditions are that the other payment was or is paid— (a) by the company ... (b) to the director ... and (c) in connection with the same event"

-- src:2915 | (4) Where the payment in question is one to which section 218 or 219 applies (payment in connection with transfer of undertaking, property or shares), the conditions are that the other payment was (or is) paid in connection with the same transfer—
-- src:2916 | (a) to the director to whom the payment in question was made, and
-- src:2917 | (b) by the company making the payment or any of its subsidiaries.
@ref s 221(4) other relevant payments where section 218 or 219 applies (src:2915-2917)
GIVEN `paid in connection with the same transfer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paid to the director to whom the payment in question was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paid by the company making the payment or any of its subsidiaries` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 221(4) the conditions are met` MEANS
    IF `paid in connection with the same transfer` AND `paid to the director to whom the payment in question was made` AND `paid by the company making the payment or any of its subsidiaries`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the conditions are that the other payment was (or is) paid in connection with the same transfer— (a) to the director ... and (b) by the company making the payment or any of its subsidiaries"

DECLARE `s 221(2) the payment in question` IS ONE OF
    `s 221(3) a payment to which section 217 applies`
    `s 221(4) a payment to which section 218 or 219 applies`
    `s 221(2) some other payment`

-- src:2910 | (2) For this purpose “other relevant payments” are payments for loss of office in relation to which the following conditions are met.
@ref s 221(2) other relevant payments (src:2910-2910)
GIVEN `the payment in question` IS A `s 221(2) the payment in question`
      `the other payment is a payment for loss of office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 221(3) the conditions are met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 221(4) the conditions are met` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 221(2) the other payment is one of the other relevant payments` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the other payment is a payment for loss of office`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“other relevant payments” are payments for loss of office in relation to which the following conditions are met"
        IF `the payment in question` EQUALS `s 221(3) a payment to which section 217 applies`
        THEN `s 221(3) the conditions are met`
        IF `the payment in question` EQUALS `s 221(4) a payment to which section 218 or 219 applies`
        THEN `s 221(4) the conditions are met`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): conditions are given for payments to which s 217, 218 or 219 applies only

-- src:2907 | (1) Approval is not required under section 217, 218 or 219 (payments requiring members' approval) if—
-- src:2908 | (a) the payment in question is made by the company or any of its subsidiaries, and
-- src:2909 | (b) the amount or value of the payment, together with the amount or value of any other relevant payments, does not exceed £200.
@ref s 221(1) small payments (src:2907-2909)
GIVEN `the payment in question is made by the company or any of its subsidiaries` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount or value of the payment` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount or value of any other relevant payments` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 221(1) approval under section 217, 218 or 219 is not required by this section` MEANS
    IF `the payment in question is made by the company or any of its subsidiaries`
       AND (`the amount or value of the payment` PLUS `the amount or value of any other relevant payments`) AT MOST `s 221(1) the sum in pounds`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if— (a) the payment in question is made by the company or any of its subsidiaries, and (b) the amount or value of the payment, together with the amount or value of any other relevant payments, does not exceed £200"

-- ======================================================================================================================
-- s 222 Payments made without approval: civil consequences
-- ======================================================================================================================

DECLARE `s 222 for whom the payment is held on trust` IS ONE OF
    `s 222(1)(a) the company making the payment`
    `s 222(2) the company whose undertaking or property is or is proposed to be transferred`
    `s 222(3)(a) the persons who have sold their shares as a result of the offer made`

-- Which of subsections (1), (2) and (3) applies: (4) "If a payment is in contravention of section 217 and section 218, subsection (2) of this section applies rather than
-- subsection (1)"; (5) "in contravention of section 217 and section 219, subsection (3) ... applies rather than subsection (1), unless the court directs otherwise".
-- src:2919 | (1) If a payment is made in contravention of section 217 (payment by company)—
-- src:2920 | (a) it is held by the recipient on trust for the company making the payment, and
-- src:2921 | (b) any director who authorised the payment is jointly and severally liable to indemnify the company that made the payment for any loss resulting from it.
@ref s 222(1) a payment in contravention of section 217 (src:2919-2921)
GIVEN `contravenes section 217` IS A BOOLEAN
      `contravenes section 218` IS A BOOLEAN
      `contravenes section 219` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court directs otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 222(1) subsection (1) applies to the payment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `contravenes section 217`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a payment is made in contravention of section 217"
        IF `contravenes section 218`
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a payment is in contravention of section 217 and section 218, subsection (2) of this section applies rather than subsection (1)"
        IF `contravenes section 219` AND (NOT `the court directs otherwise`)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a payment is in contravention of section 217 and section 219, subsection (3) of this section applies rather than subsection (1), unless the court directs otherwise"
        IF `contravenes section 219`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "unless the court directs otherwise" (what the court directs is not in the text)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:2922 | (2) If a payment is made in contravention of section 218 (payment in connection with transfer of undertaking etc), it is held by the recipient on trust for the company whose undertaking or property is or is proposed to be transferred.
@ref s 222(2) a payment in contravention of section 218 (src:2922-2922)
GIVEN `contravenes section 218` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 222(2) subsection (2) applies to the payment` MEANS
    IF `contravenes section 218`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a payment is made in contravention of section 218"

-- src:2923 | (3) If a payment is made in contravention of section 219 (payment in connection with share transfer)—
-- src:2924 | (a) it is held by the recipient on trust for persons who have sold their shares as a result of the offer made, and
-- src:2925 | (b) the expenses incurred by the recipient in distributing that sum amongst those persons shall be borne by him and not retained out of that sum.
@ref s 222(3) a payment in contravention of section 219 (src:2923-2925)
GIVEN `contravenes section 217` IS A BOOLEAN
      `contravenes section 219` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court directs otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 222(3) subsection (3) applies to the payment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `contravenes section 219`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a payment is made in contravention of section 219"
        IF `contravenes section 217` AND `the court directs otherwise`
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "subsection (3) of this section applies rather than subsection (1), unless the court directs otherwise" (what the court directs is not in the text)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:2926 | (4) If a payment is in contravention of section 217 and section 218, subsection (2) of this section applies rather than subsection (1).
-- src:2927 | (5) If a payment is in contravention of section 217 and section 219, subsection (3) of this section applies rather than subsection (1), unless the court directs otherwise.
@ref s 222(4) and (5) which subsection applies (src:2926-2927)
GIVEN `s 222(1) subsection (1) applies to the payment` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 222(2) subsection (2) applies to the payment` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 222(3) subsection (3) applies to the payment` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 222 for whom the payment is held on trust`
`s 222 the payment is held by the recipient on trust for` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 222(2) subsection (2) applies to the payment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST `s 222(2) the company whose undertaking or property is or is proposed to be transferred`
        IF `s 222(3) subsection (3) applies to the payment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST `s 222(3)(a) the persons who have sold their shares as a result of the offer made`
        IF `s 222(1) subsection (1) applies to the payment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST `s 222(1)(a) the company making the payment`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a payment is made in contravention of section 217 ... 218 ... 219" (no contravention, or the court's direction decides)

-- src:2921 | (b) any director who authorised the payment is jointly and severally liable to indemnify the company that made the payment for any loss resulting from it.
@ref s 222(1)(b) the authorising director's liability (src:2921-2921)
GIVEN `s 222(1) subsection (1) applies to the payment` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the director authorised the payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 222(1)(b) the director is jointly and severally liable to indemnify the company that made the payment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 222(1) subsection (1) applies to the payment` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `the director authorised the payment`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `s 222(1) subsection (1) applies to the payment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any director who authorised the payment is jointly and severally liable"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a payment is made in contravention of section 217 ... any director who authorised the payment" (subsection (1) does not apply, or its application is not known)

-- src:2925 | (b) the expenses incurred by the recipient in distributing that sum amongst those persons shall be borne by him and not retained out of that sum.
@ref s 222(3)(b) the recipient's expenses of distribution (src:2925-2925)
GIVEN `s 222(3) subsection (3) applies to the payment` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 222(3)(b) the expenses incurred by the recipient in distributing the sum are borne by him and not retained out of the sum` MEANS
    IF `s 222(3) subsection (3) applies to the payment` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a payment is made in contravention of section 219"
